WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.317
♫ Guadalajara

00:00:02.317 --> 00:00:06.400
♫ Guadalajara ♫

00:00:12.165 --> 00:00:15.998
- Our mariachi, Flor de
Toloache, is different

00:00:16.887 --> 00:00:18.554
than most mariachis.

00:00:20.388 --> 00:00:21.280
(cheering)

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.802
We're formed in New York City.

00:00:22.802 --> 00:00:24.509
We're all women.

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:27.325
Most people think of mariachi
as being from Mexico,

00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:29.947
as being men, as being macho,

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:33.997
and, you know, we're pretty much
opposite of all those things.

00:00:33.997 --> 00:00:37.080
(singing in Spanish)

00:00:37.964 --> 00:00:41.332
- I started my musical
career playing with a local,

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:44.015
all-male mariachi in Brooklyn.

00:00:44.015 --> 00:00:46.801
For me, it was really hard to communicate

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.006
with other male mariachis

00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:51.989
because of the machismo that's very vivid

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:55.958
in the culture and in
the genre of mariachi.

00:00:55.958 --> 00:00:56.989
♫ Ay, ay, ay ♫

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:00.953
That's kind of why I wanted to start my own group,

00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:05.158
and that led for me to
do a all-female group,

00:01:05.158 --> 00:01:07.966
because I didn't wanna
deal with men. (laughing)

00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:10.136
And it's not so much that people say,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.358
"You're not a mariachi,"

00:01:11.358 --> 00:01:13.320
but it's the fact

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.528
that they think that
we cannot play mariachi

00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:17.512
'cause we're women and were wearing pants

00:01:17.512 --> 00:01:22.007
and we have curly hair
and we don't look Mexican,

00:01:22.007 --> 00:01:24.198
or (laughing) we don't have this look

00:01:24.198 --> 00:01:25.276
that they're expecting.

00:01:25.276 --> 00:01:28.851
♫ I can't say you let me down ♫

00:01:28.851 --> 00:01:30.506
- As a women mariachi,

00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:32.830
we're technically supposed
to be wearing skirts.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.830
And, didn't work for us.

00:01:41.491 --> 00:01:43.887
- It's one of the most passionate music

00:01:43.887 --> 00:01:45.225
that I've ever heard.

00:01:45.225 --> 00:01:46.622
It's just beautiful.

00:01:46.622 --> 00:01:49.545
It's very heartfelt and I think

00:01:49.545 --> 00:01:52.712
that's what makes mariachi so special.

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:56.086
It's my dream to be able to perform

00:01:56.086 --> 00:01:58.974
and connect with people through music.

00:01:58.974 --> 00:02:01.246
I don't think I could ask for more.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:04.021
That's what keeps us going, I think.

00:02:04.021 --> 00:02:04.887
Thank you so much!

00:02:04.887 --> 00:02:06.500
Gracias, Nueva York!

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.588
- Thank you so much, everybody!

00:02:08.588 --> 00:02:09.588
We love you!

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.931
(mumbling)

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:14.181
(applause)

